<strong>Short fall nails</strong> are not the fallback version of the season. That is worth saying plainly, because almost nothing photographed for autumn nail inspiration was shot on a nail bed under half an inch. The almond tips, the coffin extensions, the dramatic negative space designs all assume length most women do not have and many do not want. <strong>Short fall nails</strong> need a different set of rules, not a lesser version of someone else's.

Those rules start with shape, not colour. Almond and coffin need free edge to actually read as almond or coffin, and most short nail beds don't have it; ask for either shape on a nail bed with limited length and a nail tech is working against the shape, not with it. Get the shape right first and the rest of the season, the rust tones, the plaid accents, the ombre, opens up properly. Get it wrong and every colour on this list will look like it is straining against the canvas rather than sitting on it.

This one lives at the top of the list for a reason: the shape decision determines whether everything that follows actually works, and it is the one thing competitor content skips entirely in favour of jumping straight to colour. <a href='/blog/fall/fall-nail-ideas'>Fall nail ideas</a> built for longer lengths are worth browsing for colour inspiration, but the shape guidance below is what makes any of it translate.

