## What Nail Shape Works Best for Short Fall Nails?

<strong>Squoval</strong> and short oval are the two shapes built for a shorter nail bed, and almond or coffin are not, because both of those require enough free edge to taper into a point or extend into a flat top. <strong>Squoval</strong> is a square shape with softened corners, holding a straight line across the tip while rounding just enough at the edges to avoid the harshness of a true square. It gives a short nail structure without demanding length it doesn't have.

