## Your Nails Were Never the Compromise

Short nails were never the version of fall you settle for while waiting for length. Once the shape is right, squoval or short oval, the colour, the finish, the single accent nail, all of it stops being an adaptation and starts being the actual choice. That's the shift this season rewards: not more nail, better decisions about the nail you have.

Book the squoval shape. Ask for the jelly finish over the flat one. Pick BIAB if glove season is coming for you either way. None of that is a workaround for <strong>short fall nails</strong>, it's simply what fall looks like when it's built for a short nail bed instead of borrowed from a long one. <strong>Short fall nails</strong> were always going to be a genuine style. This season just finally caught up to saying so.
